Z||000023||Voytek||09-14-2001||05:16 PM||||Ok, let me elaborate.  Races are like spices.  If you add just a bit to your soup, it actually tastes much better.  Of you over-do it, it starts to taste like sh*t.<P>I am NOT racist (not that anyone accused me of being) but I believe in prevention.  Leadfoot - you went out with an oriental girl - nothing wrong with that.  I was seeing a black girl for a while.<P>The point is that there would be much less racial tension and no hate crimes in our homelands if there was no one to commit them against.  I've lived in 3 countries.  In Poland (due to its communist regime at the time) 99.99999 people were Polish.  When I say polish, I mean caucasian.  Guess what?  We had no laws against hate crimes, there was no racial tension and race was NEVER an issue.<P>In Germany (where I've lived for a year) things were a bit different.  There was a lot of racial tension, partly because the incoming foreigners had no respect for local traditions, laws, etc. and partly because the local population simply did not accept foreigners.<P>What I'm saying is that races shouldn't mix to the extent that we see here in North America, and not just for the sake of the local people.  The arab man at the gas station would not have been attacked by a white man for racial reasons had he been pumping gas somewhere in the Middle East.<P>Was it his fault for being here and getting attacked?  Definitely not - he probably came here looking for a better life.<P>Do you see my point?<P>As far as I'm concerned all people are equal, but not all of them believe that they are.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000024||stsmithgt||09-14-2001||05:52 PM||||That spice example works for me.  I've had a pretty spicey line up of girls in my time. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
